5. VERDICT
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  trivial baseline      : 0.3472
  video only            : 0.3605   (+0.0132 vs trivial)
  audio only            : 0.3574   (+0.0102 vs trivial)
  audio + video         : 0.3586   (+0.0114 vs trivial)
  text control          : 0.4150   (+0.0678 vs trivial)
  text + audio + video  : 0.4277   (+0.0127 vs TEXT ALONE)

  The last line is the one that decides whether fusion is worth pursuing:
  => Audio/video add only +0.0127 on top of text — they are largely
     REDUNDANT with the transcript on this dataset. No fusion architecture
     can extract value that is not present. This is a legitimate finding:
     report the ceiling, not a fusion fix.

  => The audio/visual features carry essentially NO usable signal.
     The text control works, so the probe is sound.
     CONCLUSION: the bottleneck is FEATURE PREPROCESSING, not fusion.
     Next: diagnosis items 9 (per-utterance z-normalisation,
     create_dataset.py:378-381) and 10 (OpenFace2 vs FACET, :282).

